  "claim": "The venue in Orlando opened in the 1930's and is found west of the home venue for the Orlando City SC. The 2017 Pro Bowl was played there.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Camping World Stadium. Sentence: Camping World Stadium, also known as the Orlando Citrus Bowl, is a stadium located in Orlando, Florida.\nPage: Camping World Stadium. Sentence: The stadium is located in the West Lakes neighborhoods of Downtown Orlando, west of new sports and entertainment facilities including the Amway Center, the Dr. Phillips Center for the Performing Arts and the Orlando City Stadium.\nPage: Orlando City Stadium. Sentence: It is the home venue for the Orlando City SC, which entered Major League Soccer (MLS) as an expansion franchise in 2015, and their National Women's Soccer League (NWSL) sister club, the Orlando Pride.\nPage: 2017 Pro Bowl. Sentence: The 2017 Pro Bowl (branded as the 2017 Pro Bowl presented by Aquafina for sponsorship reasons) was the National Football League's all-star game for the 2016 season which was played at Camping World Stadium in Orlando, Florida on January 29, 2017.",
